# ALLOWLIST. This file used to be a denylist, and a denylist fails OPEN: anything added to the
# repo later ships by default. That is how the VSIX came to contain dist/dual-runtime-review.md
# (an internal architecture audit naming the weakest spots with file:lines), tmp/cleanroom-kit/**,
# .claude/settings.json, .github/workflows/publish.yml, AGENTS.md and .githooks/pre-commit.
#
# Everything is excluded by `**`, then the runtime artifacts are added back with `!`. A new
# top-level file now ships NOTHING until it is explicitly allowed here.
#
# Verify after changing this:  pnpm run vsix && unzip -l pi-code-gui-*.vsix

**

# ── the extension itself ──────────────────────────────────────────────
!dist/extension.js
!dist/webview.js

# ── webview assets (styles, icons, vendored libs the CSP loads) ───────
# Enumerated rather than `!media/**` + re-exclusions: vsce's negation re-includes the whole
# subtree and later patterns do NOT win it back, so the dev-only entry shim, the architecture
# artifacts and a 590 KB source map all shipped.
!media/style.css
!media/bundle.js
!media/marked.min.js
!media/lib/**
# Only the pi-* brand/icon assets. architecture.svg/png are docs — the README links them by
# absolute GitHub URL, so they must not be packaged.
!media/pi-*.svg
!media/pi-*.png

# ── marketplace metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!LICENSE.md
!NOTICE
!NOTICE.md
!pi-icon-light.png
!pi-icon-dark.png

# ── belt and braces ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Already excluded by `**`, but named so the intent survives a future edit that loosens the
# allowlist: never ship internal docs, agent config, CI, hooks, or tooling.
dist/**/*.md
tmp/**
.claude/**
.github/**
.githooks/**
AGENTS.md
agent-wiki/**
scripts/**
src/**
out/**
**/*.map
**/*.ts
